-- title:
--   Gauss reductions of the integral charts of X₁(M) have DVR localisations
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K'$ compatible with $L$; let $j' \in K'$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq} = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } j\text{-numerator over } \mathbb{Q})$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$. For $S$ either [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K' j'`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) or `chartAlgInf A K' j'` — the subalgebra of elements of $K'$ integral over $A[j']$, respectively over $A[j'^{-1}]$ — consider the $k$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ generated by all $r$ of the form $r = \bar{x}/\bar{y}$, where $x, y \in A[[q]]$ have $y$ with nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, some $b \in S$ satisfies $b \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$, and $\bar{x}, \bar{y}$ denote the images of $x, y$ in $k((q))$. The conclusion asserts, for both choices of $S$, that the localisation of this $k$-algebra at every maximal ideal is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is the chartwise local form of good reduction of $X_1(M)$ at a prime $p \nmid M$: the two Gauss-reduction algebras are the coordinate rings of the charts of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(M)$ over $A$, read through $q$-expansions, and the statement says that this fibre is regular at every closed point of either chart. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOne.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1), where the Noetherian one-dimensional domain with discrete valuation localisations is thereby Dedekind, hence integrally closed.
